naga: spv-in: return errors instead of panicking on malformed modules

Found by the naga `spv_parser` fuzz target. Every site below panicked on a
module that the fuzzer produced; the minimized inputs are in
`naga/tests/naga/spirv_malformed.rs` (and as fuzz-target inputs in the
suite's repro/ directory).

- `get_expr_handle` returns a `Result`: spilling an expression whose result
  type id is not a type indexed `lookup_type` and panicked.
- `parse`: a call to an id that was never defined as a function unwrapped
  `lookup_function`.
- unary/binary/comparison ops, `OpSMod`, `OpBitField{Insert,SExtract,UExtract}`
  on non-numeric operand types unwrapped `scalar_kind()`; switch selectors of
  non-integer type hit `unimplemented!`; all return the new
  `Error::InvalidOperandType`.
- `OpCompositeConstruct` with no constituents indexed `components[0]`.
- `OpCompositeInsert` with an index past the end of the composite.
- `OpSwitch` on an undefined selector id; `OpGroupNonUniformQuadSwap` with a
  direction other than 0..=2 (`unreachable!`).
- `OpPhi`: undefined source ids, predecessor labels that are not blocks of
  the function, and invalid types of spilled sources.
- `OpBranchConditional` to a label that already has a body asserted (debug
  builds only); now an `InvalidEdgeClassification` error.
- image sampling/fetch/write with coordinates that are not a numeric scalar or
  vector (`unreachable!`).
- image fetch/write with integer coordinates on arrayed (or garbage-extended)
  images expected an integer coordinate vector type that only exists if the
  module happens to declare it; the type is now inserted. This also affects
  valid modules.
- comparison sampling from a binding array of sampled images: binding arrays
  are tracked for comparison sampling but `patch_comparison_type` only
  handled images and samplers (`unreachable!`). It now flips the element
  type. This also affects valid modules.
- `OpSampledImage` whose sampler is a global that is not tracked as a sampler
  unwrapped `handle_sampling`.
- atomics: `Access` on non-arrays, `AccessIndex` on non-structs/arrays or past
  the last struct member, and atomics on a whole struct global
  (`unreachable!` in `atomic_upgrade`) are errors now.
- `process_entry_point`: culling unused built-ins of an output struct called
  `UniqueArena::replace` with a type that already existed in the arena
  (assertion); keep the original type in that case.
